---
/**
 * `/terms` — DRAFT for attorney review.
 *
 * The load-bearing point is the first one: nothing here is an offer. The site
 * publishes six room rates, a fee, an SLA and a 2027 product commitment, and none
 * of those should bind before an agreement is signed.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, property, home } from '../data/site.config';
const updated = '27 July 2026';
---
<Base title="Terms" description="Terms of use for this website, and what the information on it does and does not commit us to.">
  <section class="wrap stack measure">
    <h1 class="display-l">Terms</h1>
    <p class="draft"><strong>Draft, pending legal review.</strong> Last updated {updated}.</p>

    <h2>This site is information, not an offer</h2>
    <p>
      Rates, availability, services and dates on this site are published in good faith and can change.
      Nothing here is an offer to lease, and nothing binds either of us until there is a signed
      agreement. Submitting the inquiry form does not reserve a room.
    </p>

    <h2>Pre-leasing</h2>
    <p>
      The house is being renovated. Occupancy is targeted for {property.applications.forOccupancy} and no
      specific day is committed until we say so in writing. Services shown with a future date are not
      running yet — the date is when we expect them to start, not a guarantee.
    </p>

    <h2>An inquiry is not an application</h2>
    <p>
      The form on this site starts a conversation. The rental application is a separate document,
      completed off-site, and it is that process — not this website — that decides whether a room is
      offered.
    </p>

    <h2>Rates</h2>
    <p>
      Room rates follow the published rule: {home.terms.roomPricingRule} Unit and whole-building rates
      are quoted on inquiry. Rates can be adjusted for length of stay, multiple rooms and agency
      bookings; any adjustment follows criteria applied the same way to everyone.
    </p>

    <h2>Fair housing</h2>
    <p>{site.legal.eho}</p>

    <h2>No affiliation with health systems</h2>
    <p>
      We name nearby hospitals as landmarks and measure travel times to them. We are not affiliated
      with, endorsed by, or in partnership with any health system, and nothing here should be read to
      suggest otherwise.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      Distances and travel times are measured, and the method and date are stated where they appear.
      Traffic and circumstances vary — confirm anything you intend to rely on. Where a fact is not yet
      known, this site shows a visible placeholder rather than an estimate.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party content</h2>
    <p>
      The commute page embeds a map from Google, subject to Google's own terms. We link to other
      businesses; we do not control their sites.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>{site.contact.name} · {site.contact.email} · {site.contact.phone}</p>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  section { padding-block: var(--s12) var(--s8); }
  .draft { border-left: 3px solid var(--brick); padding-left: var(--s4); }
  h2 { margin-top: var(--s8); }
</style>
